<main id="main">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="ph-media"><img class="zoom" src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="631" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="shell ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="/tennessee-claim-tools/">Claim tools</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">RCV/ACV Holdback Calculator</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free calculator · runs in your browser</p><h1>RCV vs. ACV Depreciation and Holdback Calculator</h1><p class="lede">Replacement cost policies usually pay twice: an actual cash value check now, then the held-back depreciation once repairs are done. Build your item list and see how the money splits.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="shell"><noscript><p class="note">This calculator needs JavaScript. Everything runs in your browser and nothing is stored.</p></noscript>
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="dep">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Depreciation &amp; holdback calculator</span><i>Add as many items as you need</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <div class="table-wrap items-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Replacement cost ($)</th><th>Age (yrs)</th><th>Life (yrs)</th><th>ACV</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><input name="item" value="Architectural shingle roof" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="18500" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="9" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="30" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr><tr><td><input name="item" value="Interior paint — living areas" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="2400" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="4" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="10" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr><tr><td><input name="item" value="Carpet — two bedrooms" aria-label="Item"></td><td><input name="rcv" inputmode="decimal" value="1850" aria-label="Replacement cost"></td><td><input name="age" inputmode="decimal" value="6" aria-label="Age in years"></td><td><input name="life" inputmode="decimal" value="10" aria-label="Expected life in years"></td><td class="mono" data-o="row">$0</td><td><button type="button" class="x" aria-label="Remove row">×</button></td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-add data-run>+ Add item</button></div>
      <div class="row2">
        <div><label for="d-ded">Deductible ($)</label><input id="d-ded" name="deduct" inputmode="decimal" value="1000"></div>
        <div><label for="d-cap">Maximum depreciation</label><select id="d-cap" name="cap"><option value="50">50%</option><option value="70">70%</option><option value="80" selected>80%</option><option value="90">90%</option></select><span class="hint">Most estimates cap depreciation; check yours.</span></div>
      </div>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="nonrec"> My policy pays actual cash value only (no recoverable depreciation)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr))">
      <div class="out-big"><small>First check (ACV − deductible)</small><b data-o="first">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-big"><small>Held back until repairs</small><b data-o="held">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-big"><small>Total if fully recovered</small><b data-o="total">$0</b></div>
      <div class="out-rows" style="grid-column:1/-1">
        <div><span>Replacement cost (RCV)</span><b data-o="rcv">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Total depreciation</span><b data-o="dep">$0</b></div>
        <div><span>Depreciation as share of RCV</span><b data-o="deppct">0%</b></div>
        <div><span>Actual cash value (ACV)</span><b data-o="acv">$0</b></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms; they aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Default figures are illustrative.</p></div></section>
<div class="shell layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>The method behind the numbers</h2>
<p>Each line uses straight-line depreciation: age divided by expected life, capped at the maximum you pick. Carrier estimates may use condition adjustments or treat some charges as non-depreciable, so treat the output as a planning figure.</p>
<h2>Useful life ranges</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical range</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th>Architectural asphalt shingles</th><td>25–30 years</td></tr><tr><th>Three-tab shingles</th><td>18–25 years</td></tr><tr><th>Standing-seam metal roof</th><td>40–60 years</td></tr><tr><th>Interior paint</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Carpet</th><td>8–12 years</td></tr><tr><th>Central HVAC condenser</th><td>12–18 years</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>Collecting the holdback</h2>
<p>Most policies release recoverable depreciation after repairs are finished within a stated time. Send final invoices and photos. The <a href="/tennessee-claim-tools/claim-deadline-calendar/">claim deadline calendar</a> can remind you before the window closes.</p>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can labor be depreciated?</summary><div class="a"><p>Treatment of labor depreciation varies by policy form and by court decisions in different jurisdictions. Ask the carrier to explain in writing how labor was handled in your estimate.</p></div></details><details><summary>What happens if I don’t repair?</summary><div class="a"><p>Under most replacement cost policies, you keep the ACV payment but may not collect the held-back depreciation.</p></div></details></div>
